  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x,$ then $f(x)=$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{\u2032}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\text{\u00a0arcsec\u00a0}x-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
